---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Doc from '../components/legal/Doc.astro';
const updated = '30 October 2026';
// Shows a draft note and keeps the page out of search until the placeholders are filled (design/legal/README.md).
const draft = true;
---

<Base title="Privacy policy · Comarket" description="What Comarket collects, why, who processes it, how long we keep it, and your privacy rights." stage="none" noindex={draft}>
  <Doc
    title="Privacy policy"
    lede="What we collect, why, who helps us, how long we keep it, and how to see or delete it."
    updated={updated}
    draft={draft}
    current="/privacy"
  >
    <div class="short">
      <b>The short version</b>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't sell your personal information or share it for advertising, and we use no third-party ad trackers.</li>
        <li>Visitors in the EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked before any analytics cookie is set.</li>
        <li>Email <a href="mailto:[[CONTACT EMAIL]]">[[CONTACT EMAIL]]</a> to see, correct or delete your data.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Comarket is run by [[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]], a [[STATE OF FORMATION]] company at [[REGISTERED ADDRESS]] ("Comarket", "we",
      "us"). This policy covers comarket.si, its subdomains (including storefronts), the waitlist, the Comarket platform and
      our emails.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>When</th><th>What we collect</th><th>Why</th><th>Kept for</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>You join the waitlist</td>
            <td>Email; brand or creator; your website and brand name, or your handle and platform; pass number; date; for brands, the fee rates you were shown</td>
            <td>To hold your place, email you when it opens, and honor the rates you saw</td>
            <td>Until you ask us to remove it, or 24 months if you don't open an account</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You join from a link</td>
            <td>Campaign tags in the link (utm_), the referring page, your country (from our host, not stored as an IP address), and the pass number in a referral link</td>
            <td>To know how people find us and credit referrals</td>
            <td>As long as the waitlist entry</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You answer the optional questions</td>
            <td>What you sell, how you charge, your audience size or topic</td>
            <td>To prepare your account</td>
            <td>As long as the waitlist entry</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You type a website or handle</td>
            <td>The website and the public name, color and icon on its homepage, or the handle</td>
            <td>To build a preview, or check a handle is free</td>
            <td>Previews: 24 hours in a cache. Handles: not stored unless you join</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You browse, with analytics on</td>
            <td>A random visitor ID (cookie), which page version you saw, and simple events (which side you chose, whether you built a preview, used a calculator, or saved or shared your pass)</td>
            <td>To learn which pages work and test prices</td>
            <td>13 months</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Any visit</td>
            <td>IP address and browser signals, handled by our host Cloudflare, including its bot check on our forms</td>
            <td>Security and stopping bots</td>
            <td>Cloudflare's request logs, a few days. We don't store IP addresses</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You open a brand account</td>
            <td>Your team's names and emails, company and billing details, offers and approvals, and the Stripe data in the next row</td>
            <td>To run the Brand Agreement and bill you</td>
            <td>The account's life, then 7 years for billing records</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You connect Stripe as a brand</td>
            <td>For buyers who start a checkout from a storefront: email, phone and card fingerprint (a code Stripe derives, never the card number), checked against your Stripe customers; payment, refund and dispute records</td>
            <td>To decide whether a sale counts and calculate fees, as your service provider under the <a href="/dpa">DPA</a></td>
            <td>Identifiers: until the check is done. Records of counted sales: 7 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You open a creator account</td>
            <td>Profile, handle, linked social profiles and their public stats, offers, storefront content, sales and earnings; identity, tax and payout details collected by Stripe (we don't see your full bank account number)</td>
            <td>To run the Creator Agreement, pay you and file tax forms</td>
            <td>The account's life, then 7 years for payout and tax records</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You visit a storefront</td>
            <td>Which storefront you came from, and when you started checkout</td>
            <td>To credit the right creator</td>
            <td>Until the brand's refund and dispute periods end</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>You email us</td>
            <td>Your message and email</td>
            <td>To answer you</td>
            <td>24 months</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Software decides whether a sale counts, which affects what a creator earns and a brand pays. Anyone affected can ask a
      person to review a decision at [[CONTACT EMAIL]]. We tell creators why a sale didn't count, but never who the buyer
      was. When you buy from a brand, the brand's own privacy policy covers your purchase.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Service providers,</b> only to run Comarket: Cloudflare (hosting, bot checks), Neon (database), Resend (email), Stripe (billing, payouts, identity and tax forms), and our email and office software. All are in the United States.</li>
      <li><b>Brands and creators:</b> a brand sees the profile, public stats and results of creators it works with; a creator sees the brand's offer. Neither sees a buyer's identity through us.</li>
      <li><b>When the law requires it,</b> to prevent fraud or harm, or in a sale of our business.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.</p>

    <h2>Your US privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      Residents of California and other states with privacy laws (including Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia, Texas and
      Oregon) can ask to know what we collect, get a copy, correct it or delete it, and appeal if we refuse. We give these
      rights to everyone in the US. We don't sell or share personal information, so there is nothing to opt out of, and we
      use creators' tax IDs only to pay them and file tax forms. Using your rights never changes how we treat you.
    </p>
    <p>
      In California's categories, we collect identifiers (email, handle, visitor ID), commercial information (fee rates,
      sales and earnings), internet activity (pages and events), approximate location (country) and professional
      information (your business, platform and audience). Sources, purposes and retention are in the table above.
    </p>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:[[CONTACT EMAIL]]">[[CONTACT EMAIL]]</a> from the address you used with us. We may ask for a little
      more to confirm it's you, and answer within 45 days. An authorized agent may ask for you with your written permission.
      To appeal a decision, reply to our answer.
    </p>

    <h2>Visitors in the EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
    <p>
      We process your information to take steps you ask for (the waitlist, your account), with your consent (analytics
      cookies and the optional questions, which you can withdraw at any time), for our legitimate interests (security,
      knowing how people find us, crediting referrals), and to meet legal duties. You can ask to access, correct, delete,
      restrict or port your data, or object to processing, by emailing [[CONTACT EMAIL]], and you can complain to your local
      data protection authority. Your information is processed in the United States under the European Commission's
      standard contractual clauses or an equivalent safeguard.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>Our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> lists every cookie we set and how to change your choice.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Connections are encrypted, the database is reachable only by our server code, analytics use a random ID instead of
      your name or IP address, and access is limited to people who need it. If a breach affects you, we'll tell you as the law
      requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Comarket is for adults. You must be 18 to join the waitlist or open an account. We don't knowingly collect information
      from children under 13, and will delete it if we learn we have.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We post changes here with a new date, and email you first about any that matter.</p>
  </Doc>
  <Footer />
</Base>
